= My favourite food -> FRIED CAULIFLOWER

== Ingredients
* 1 head of cauliflower (20.90 CZK)
* 1 kg of potatoes (10.30 CZK)
* 200 g of breadcrumbs (5.60 CZK)
* 200 ml of canola oil (4.80 CZK)
* 100 g flour (0.80 CZK)
* 120 g tartar sauce (7.50 CZK)
* 2 eggs (12 CZK)
* 2 tablespoons chopped chives (4.60 CZK)
* 1 tablespoon butter (4.60 CZK)
* salt

== Procedure
1 Peel the potatoes, cut them in half, and boil them in salted water until tender. Once cooked, drain the potatoes and let them cool out for 10 minutes. Then add a tablespoon of butter and mix in the chives.

2 Clean the cauliflower and cut out the stem from the bottom with a knife (do not discard it). Then separate the cauliflower into florets. Bring salted water to a boil in a pot. Add the cauliflower in two or three batches (depends on a size of a cauliflower) and boil for about 5 minutes until cauliflower is semi-soft. Drain the parboiled cauliflower.

3 Prepare a bowl with flour, breadcrumbs, and eggs beaten with a 10 ml of milk. Season the eggs with salt and a pepper. Coat the cauliflower florets one by one in flour, then in the egg mixture, and finally in the breadcrumbs.

4 Pour oil into a frying pan or wide saucepan. The oil should be 1 to 2 cm deep. Gradually heat the oil to a temperature of about 170 °C. Add the coated cauliflower pieces one by one and fry on both sides until golden brown. Set the fried cauliflower aside on a paper towel. Serve with boiled potatoes and tartar sauce.

